{"hw":"προσακούω","html":"<div class=\"lex-entry\"><h4 class=\"lex-hw gk\">προσακούω</h4><span class=\"lex-orth gk\">προσακούω</span>, <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">A</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">hear besides,</b> <span class=\"lex-itype gk\">τι</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">X.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">HG</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">3.4.1</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">II</span> as <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Pass.</span> </span> of <span class=\"gk\">προσαγορεύω, τοιαῦτα π.</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">to be addressed</b> in such terms, ib. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.4.22</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Plu.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">2.71e</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">812e</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἐπαινέσας προσακούω εἴρων</span> I <b class=\"lex-tr\">am called..,</b> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">J.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">BJ</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.26.2</span> </span>.</div></div>"}